        <mxCell id="b30" parent="1" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#FFFFFF;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=11;" value="2" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="24" width="24" x="423" y="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="x46" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#545B64;fontStyle=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;" value="&lt;div&gt;1&amp;nbsp; Kiro writes the daily user activity report (CSV) at 02:00 UTC (prefix kiro/, SSE-S3).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2&amp;nbsp; The CID collector Lambda pulls the report at 03:00 UTC.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3&amp;nbsp; The collector writes the report to the Data Collection bucket, partitioned by account_id.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4&amp;nbsp; The Kiro Usage Analytics normalizer Lambda pulls the report at 03:15 UTC (patches P1, P2).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;5&amp;nbsp; The normalizer writes the normalized copy to the results bucket.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;6&amp;nbsp; The identity-map Lambda assumes the customer&#39;s read-only role (ExternalId, patch P3).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;7&amp;nbsp; The role reads the user list from IAM Identity Center.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;8&amp;nbsp; User names and emails are written to the identity-map bucket.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;9&amp;nbsp; Kiro emits a data event for each request (not yet verified, OQ-1).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;10&amp;nbsp; The trail delivers the logs to the CloudTrail bucket in the observability management account.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;11&amp;nbsp; Prompt logs (full text) stay in the customer account; the observability management account cannot read them.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;12&amp;nbsp; Data Exports in the payer account delivers CUR 2.0 to the observability management account.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;13&amp;nbsp; Athena reads the buckets through the Glue tables.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;14&amp;nbsp; SPICE refreshes at 04:00 UTC.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;15&amp;nbsp; Dashboards: CUDOS (cost), CID Kiro (licenses), Kiro Usage Analytics (usage), Audit (requests).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;16&amp;nbsp; Viewers open the dashboards.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;17&amp;nbsp; The freshness-check Lambda runs at 05:00 UTC and sends an SNS alert when data is late.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Dashed line: a Lambda in the observability management account reads customer resources (pull).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Kiro Usage Analytics: the aws-samples/sample-kiro-user-analytics-quicksight-dashboard repo, one deployment per customer.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The customer&#39;s payer account, Kiro account and Identity Center account can be separate accounts.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="618" x="20" y="900" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="x47" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=44;fontColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;" value="Kiro Enterprise&lt;br&gt;Monitoring" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="440" x="690" y="960" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
